+# RFP Reference — Full Extract (Darden RegIntel Studio)
+
+Optional appendix. `rfp-brief.md` and `discovery-call-transcript.md` are
+the two documents you actually need to start — this is the fuller raw RFP
+detail behind them, for when you want to check a specific fact rather than
+work only from the curated summary. Trimmed of content irrelevant to this
+exercise (e.g. the client's general HR handbook policies) — everything below
+is real RFP/scope detail.
+
+## Scope of Services — Requested Platform Capabilities
+
+Development and implementation of an AI-powered Regulatory Intelligence &
+Compliance Decision Platform (RegIntel Studio) performing:
+
+- **Regulatory Monitoring** — continuously detect new/changing laws from
+  agreed source lists, structured event records with provenance.
+- **Relevance Determination** — classify applicability by topic,
+  jurisdiction, brand, location, employee group, effective date; assess
+  operational/HR/wage-and-hour impact.
+- **Action Recommendation** — draft required actions, communications,
+  posting notices, meeting guidance, escalation paths.
+- **Communication Drafting & Targeting** — audience-specific updates (Legal
+  Updates, manager instructions, executive summaries) with recommended
+  distribution.
+- **Knowledge Retention & Learning** — capture final SME decisions,
+  overrides, and rationale to improve future classification/recommendation.
+- **Workflow Management** — intake, initial review, HITL triage/impact
+  assessment, tracking/action-plan documentation, review/approval of
+  drafts, evidence collection, closeout, publishing, reporting.
+- **Dashboard & Reporting** — centralized view of regulations, obligations,
+  implementation status, risk exposure, audit readiness, key metrics.
+- **Template Management** — Legal Update templates with version control.
+
+## Requested Teams, Skillsets, Roles
+
+- Engagement Lead / Product Owner
+- AI Solution Architect
+- Lead Agent Engineer
+- Agent Engineer
+- Data Engineer
+- UX / Workflow Designer
+- Delivery Manager / Scrum Lead
+
+EPAM "Core Pod" sized at ~3.7 FTEs. Full delivery team (EPAM + Darden +
+Microsoft) ~8–10 active participants during the 12-week MVP.
+
+## Delivery Approach — 12-Week MVP Build Plan (as proposed in the source deck)
+
+- **Weeks 1–2 — Foundation**: source inventory and use-case intake, Foundry
+  project setup, event schema and tracker ingestion design, guardrails,
+  access, evaluation plan.
+- **Weeks 3–5 — Monitor + Relevance**: initial source connectors, change
+  detection workflow, relevance classification, discarded-law review queue.
+- **Weeks 6–9 — Assess + Act**: applicability/risk reasoning, action
+  recommendation agent, communication templates, human review workflow.
+- **Weeks 10–12 — Evaluate + Handoff**: parallel run against manual
+  process, quality/hallucination testing, SME feedback loop, production
+  plan and expansion backlog.
+
+### Expansion Timeline (post-MVP)
+
+- Weeks 1–12: Wage & Hour MVP — prove full decision pipeline.
+- Weeks 13–20: Topic expansion — leave laws, scheduling.
+- Weeks 21–28: Knowledge learning — decision reuse, pattern recognition,
+  confidence-based review rules.
+- Weeks 29–40: Enterprise scale — broader domains, analytics, operational
+  dashboards, predictive compliance signals.
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- Other sites/locations beyond the initial scope, for now.
+- Regulation types outside wage-and-hour, sick leave, paid family/medical
+  leave, wage transparency, employment, compliance training.
+- Integration with any application beyond what's explicitly listed below.
+- RegIntel does not replace legal judgment — final authority for
+  interpretation, risk posture, and rollout always sits with
+  Legal/Compliance.
+- HRC Analysts own HITL review: confirming applicability, deciding to track
+  or close items, providing rationale.
+- HRC/Legal/business stakeholders must review and approve draft Legal
+  Updates and compliance actions before finalization/communication.
+- Darden provides: the source list, one representative use case, keywords
+  and topic instructions, and the current Excel tracker.
+- Humans audit and can override every agent recommendation, always.
+
+## Technology
+
+**Current stack:** listservs, government websites, agency bulletins, legal
+alerts, industry updates, Excel tracker, templated emails, distribution
+lists.
+
+**Target stack:** Azure, Azure AI Foundry, Python, Azure AI Search
+(hybrid/vector index), App/Review Portal (SME queue), RegIntel Dashboard,
+conversational interface, SharePoint, Blob Storage, Microsoft Entra ID,
+Prompt Flow/evaluations.
+
+**Client-specific integrations:** Littler email communication, MRL (Master
+Restaurant List), PeopleSoft, My Compliance Hub, Communications Team.
+
+**COTS integrations:** Microsoft 365, Teams, Outlook, SharePoint, Equifax
+Compliance Center, LMS, GovDocs.
+
+## Non-Functional Requirements
+
+**Compliance & Governance:** audit readiness, traceability & controls,
+prompt versioning, evaluation scorecards, source provenance, model
+monitoring, approval history, audit trail, documented rationale for
+decisions, version control on legal update templates.
+
+**Security:** guardrails against untrusted/adversarial input — the
+Monitoring Agent's source content (government sites, listservs, agency
+bulletins) is fetched from parties Darden doesn't control, and must be
+treated as data to classify, never as instructions the model follows.
+
+**Reliability & Accuracy:** trust in the system, safety net for one-off
+cases, continuous improvement from expert decisions, quality/hallucination
+testing, accuracy, confidence in relevance classification.
+
+**Usability & HITL:** human oversight, transparency (why laws are deemed
+irrelevant, not just why they're flagged), ability to audit/override,
+human review for both applicable *and* discarded regulations, SME control
+over final interpretation/escalation thresholds, approval required before
+release, prioritization of review items.
+
+**Performance & Scalability:** scalable growth across jurisdictions,
+latency, throughput.
+
+**Maintainability:** self-contained/continuously improved agent tasks,
+reusable knowledge and evaluation data, repeatable decision intelligence
+system, modular ("componentized agentic capability") architecture.
+
+## What EPAM's Proposal Must Include (Response Package)
+
+- Technical proposal
+- Viability and scope definition
+- MVP timeline and staffing
+- Foundry architecture view
+
+## Evaluation Notes
+
+- Key evaluation criteria named in the client's vendor-selection policy:
+  Quality, Price, Availability, Service.
+- Proposals are ideally selected via a competitive bidding process.
+- No explicit scoring weights are specified.
+- Standard vendor-conflict rules apply (no active employees or
+  recently-departed employees acting as vendors) — not directly relevant to
+  solutioning, included here only for completeness.
+
+## Abbreviations
+
+- **AKI** — Agentic Knowledge Initiative
+- **HITL** — Human-in-the-Loop
+- **MRL** — Master Restaurant List
+- **Reg Intel** — Regulatory Intelligence
+- **RegIntel Studio** — the internal AI agent sitting between regulation
+  and operations
+- **FMLA** — Family and Medical Leave Act
+- **USERRA** — Uniformed Services Employment and Re-employment Act of 1994
